  "model_type": [
   "gemma4_unified",
   "gemma4_unified_text"
  ]
 },
 "verified": {
  "transformers": "5.18.0",
  "date": "2026-10-05",
  "by": "reverse-model agent",
  "check": "tests/spec_conformance_test.py gemma4_unified",
  "note": "Embedding (sqrt(d_model)), all per-layer q/k/v projections, every block output and the logits match the eager library run at 0.0 (tol 1e-4). Covers both layer types (sliding: default RoPE + sliding-window causal mask; full: proportional RoPE, partial_rotary_factor 0.25, plain causal mask), the scale-less v RMSNorm, gelu_pytorch_tanh MLP and the per-layer layer_scalar. The repo is google/gemma-4-12B-it, a multimodal Gemma4UnifiedForConditionalGeneration: this family spec draws the language decoder only; the vision/audio embedders (model.embed_vision, model.embed_audio, model.vision_embedder.*, 11 tensors) stay unbound. The repo's text_config has attention_k_eq_v=true, so its 8 full_attention layers carry no v_proj and reuse the raw k projection as value: that branch is drawn and bound (k -> value = k -> v_norm), but the tiny gate config sets attention_k_eq_v=false (the library harness reads self_attn.v_proj on every layer, and a shared-kv layer has no v_proj to read), so the alternative path is not numerically gated here. Repo-only final_logit_softcapping=30.0 is not applied (no top-level post-head node in the spec; absent in the gate config); num_kv_shared_layers=0 and use_double_wide_mlp=false are inactive in this repo and not drawn."
